addresses are in a contiguous block starting at this address and
containing BOARD-MAC-ADDRESS-NUM number of addresses. The format
of this parameter is 0xXXXXXXXXXXXX, 12 hex digits starting with
'0x'.This parameter is stored in a static board manufacturing
area at the top of the boot flash.␀The number of MAC addresses assigned to the on-chip network
ports. See BOARD-MAC-ADDRESS for the actual MAC address numeric
value.This parameter is stored in a static board manufacturing
area at the top of the boot flash.␀Index mapping is like ID0-RPM0 LMAC0, ID1 - RPM0 LMAC1 ..
ID4 - RPM1 LMAC0 etc.
The format of this parameter is 0xXXXXXXXXXXXX,
12 hex digits starting with '0x'.This parameter is stored in a
static board manufacturing area at the top of the boot flash.␀The number of MAC addresses assigned to the on-chip network
ports. See BOARD-MAC-ADDRESS-ID for further details.
This parameter is stored in a static board
manufacturing area at the top of the boot flash.␀This specifies a watchdog timer should run during boot and reset
the chip if boot hangs for some reason. The timeout is specified
in milliseconds. Zero disables the watchdog.␀Allow a sequence of MDIO writes to be performed during boot. Each
string in the list line is executed in sequence. The MDIO write
format is:
    clause,bus_id,phy_id,device,location,val
    sleep,ms
    gpio,gpio_num,state
clause   = MDIO clause for the write (22 or 45)
bus_id   = MDIO bus to use
phy_id   = MDIO address
device   = Clause 45 internal device address, zero for clause 22
location = MDIO register
val      = Value to write
sleep,ms = This on a line delays for 'ms' milliseconds
gpio,... = This sets the state of a GPIO gpio_num to 0 or 1␀Specify devices external to the chip that can't be probed through
PCIe or USB. Generally these are devices connect to TWSI or
GPIOs. The format of this is list of strings where each string
represents an external device. The format of each string varies
based on the device. See the EBF manual for the details.␀Specify the mapping for the MUX in Retimer.
Each mapping provides information on GSERM, lane and in/out MUX
channels that are involved in connecting GSERM's Rx and Tx paths
There are two string entries per each MUX, as each MUX can switch
between two SerDes/lanes. Format of each entry is:
	gserm=<#gserm>,lane=<#lane>,map=0xhhhh
where:
	- #gserm (int) is an index of the gserm to be connected
	- #lane (int) is a gserm lane index
	- map contains 4 nibles: 0x Rx_in|Rx_out|Tx_in|Tx_out
␀Choose which GSERM will be enabled by a Retimer MUX.␀Allow a selection of SMI bus for integrated switch.
0 = SMI Bus 0
1 = SMI Bus 1␀Allow a selection of SMI bus for stand alone switch.
0 = SMI Bus 0
1 = SMI Bus 1␀Allow a selection of PEM Port used for Aldrin3M Connection
    Allowable values of 0 to 5, or -1 (not connected)
␀Allow a selection of SSMI Slave Address for switch.
Select a slave address from 0 to 7, default is 7␀Allow a selection of Device Init Done Pin From Switch. The switch firmware
Sets this pin when it is ready to receive firmware over SMI interface.
    Allowable values of 0 to 76 (64 for EBB106)
␀Allow a selection of Device Interrupt Pin From Switch. The switch firmware
Sets this pin when it is asserting an interrupt to the Octeon.
    Allowable values of 0 to 76 (64 for EBB106)
␀Configure the switch in u-boot or CPSS
0 = Switch will be configured by CPSS
1 = Switch will be configured by u-boot
␀Reset Switch before booting Kernel
1 = Reset Switch
0 = Do not reset Switch (hitless support) 
␀PCIe reference clock selection
0 = Local Reference Clock - Group 1
1 = External Reference Clock - Group 2
␀EBF Version information.␀Controls the cores used by the EBF. Zero means all cores.␀Timeout for the boot menu in seconds.␀Device used to boot, string representation of RST_BOOT_METHOD_E.
This is filled by the EBF with the device used to boot␀EBF trace level. This is a bitmask of the enumeration defined in
ebf-warn.h. Each bit turns on tracing of a specific EBF
component.␀Boolean flag for skipping TIM version processing
    0 = Do not skip (default)
    1 = Skip␀Allow a sequence of TWSI writes to be performed during boot. Each
string in the list line is executed in sequence when a key is pressed
while boot EBF to disable external wdog. The TWSI write
format is:
    twsi_id,dev_addr,internal_addr,num_bytes,ia_width_bytes,data
twsi_id        = TWSI bus to use
dev_addr       = TWSI bus address
internal_addr  = TWSI internal address, zero if not used
num_bytes      = Number of bytes to write (1-8)
ia_width_bytes = Internal address width in bytes (0-2)
data           = Data to write as a 64bit number
␀Determine if internal PCIe ECAMs support Enhanced Allocation(EA):
    0 = Enhanced Allocation is not supported
    1 = Enhanced Allocation is supported␀Enforcing stronger PCIe ordering. Use this option if a PCIe card
is having compatibility issues.
    0 = Don't wait for commit, default for best performance.
    1 = Wait for commit, use conservative ordering.␀Specifies the preset request vector (PCIERCX_GEN3_EQ_CTL/PCIERCX_CFG554[PRV]).
Requesting of presets during the initial part of the EQ master phase.
Encoding scheme as follows:
    Bit [15:0] = 0x0: No preset is requested and evaluated in the EQ master phase.
    Bit [i] = 1: Preset=i is requested and evaluated in the EQ master phase.
    0000000000000000: No preset req/evaluated in EQ master phase
    00000xxxxxxxxxx1: Preset 0 req/evaluated in EQ master phase
    00000xxxxxxxxx1x: Preset 1 req/evaluated in EQ master phase
    00000xxxxxxxx1xx: Preset 2 req/evaluated in EQ master phase
    00000xxxxxxx1xxx: Preset 3 req/evaluated in EQ master phase
    00000xxxxxx1xxxx: Preset 4 req/evaluated in EQ master phase
    00000xxxxx1xxxxx: Preset 5 req/evaluated in EQ master phase
    00000xxxx1xxxxxx: Preset 6 req/evaluated in EQ master phase
    00000xxx1xxxxxxx: Preset 7 req/evaluated in EQ master phase
    00000xx1xxxxxxxx: Preset 8 req/evaluated in EQ master phase
    00000x1xxxxxxxxx: Preset 9 req/evaluated in EQ master phase
    000001xxxxxxxxxx: Preset 10 req/evaluated in EQ master phase
    All other encodings: Reserved
Parameters:
